1
00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:03,500
Hello there! Are you ready to go?

2
00:00:04,000 --> 00:00:06,800
Almost. I just need to pick up my keys.

3
00:00:07,200 --> 00:00:10,000
Hold on, the train leaves at 7:45, right?

4
00:00:10,500 --> 00:00:13,500
- Right.
- Then we should set off now.

5
00:00:14,000 --> 00:00:17,000
<i>She always says that, and we're never late.</i>

6
00:00:17,500 --> 00:00:20,500
Did you turn off the lights in the kitchen?

7
00:00:21,000 --> 00:00:24,000
Yes. And I asked Sam to look after the cat.

8
00:00:24,500 --> 00:00:28,000
What if we run out of time
at the station?

9
00:00:28,500 --> 00:00:31,500
We won't. Don't give up before we even start.

10
00:00:32,000 --> 00:00:35,000
I still can't figure out how to read this ticket.

11
00:00:35,500 --> 00:00:38,500
Platform four, carriage "B", seat 12.

12
00:00:39,000 --> 00:00:42,500
Let's find out where the café is first.

13
00:00:43,000 --> 00:00:46,000
Coffee sounds perfect. I barely slept.

14
00:00:46,500 --> 00:00:50,000
You should get up earlier, not later!

15
00:00:50,500 --> 00:00:54,000
<b>Next train:</b> 7:45 to the coast.

16
00:00:54,500 --> 00:00:58,000
We'll come back on Sunday evening, I promise.

17
00:00:58,500 --> 00:01:02,000
Can we put off the museum until tomorrow?

18
00:01:02,500 --> 00:01:06,000
Sure. Today is for the sea, the sun and nothing else.

19
00:01:06,500 --> 00:01:10,000
Look! The train is already here.

20
00:01:10,500 --> 00:01:14,000
Quick, grab your bag. Let's go!

21
00:01:15,000 --> 00:01:19,000
This is a very long subtitle line to check how the overlay wraps text when somebody talks for a while.

22
00:01:20,000 --> 00:01:24,000
Finally. Window seats, as promised.

23
00:01:25,000 --> 00:01:29,000
Wake me up when we see the sea.
